{{#is_alert}}Every cycle in the last 15 minutes had at least one enabled collector fail (value {{value}}); opt-in ones such as SD-Access fabric or security count too.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_no_data}}No data means the check is not running or not completing.{{/is_no_data}}
{{^is_recovery}}
Look first in the Agent log for `Catalyst Center ... collection failed` or `Unexpected failure collecting Catalyst Center ...`, or run `datadog-agent check cisco_catalyst_center`. The first may include the `x-correlation-id` for Cisco TAC.

If [`cisco_catalyst_center.device.count`](/metric/explorer?exp_metric=cisco_catalyst_center.device.count&exp_scope=catalyst_center_host:{{catalyst_center_host.name}}) is still arriving, the appliance and login are fine and a later collector is failing.{{/is_recovery}}
